andon gong what so this is  very counter to what the 2011 anime  tells us quite polar opposites really  because in episode one as gon is packing  to leave mito very specifically reminds  gon that his father abandoned him and  when we do get to the conversation  outside their dialogue has changed  completely instead of revealing the  truth that jing did not in fact abandon  gon mito instead just makes gon promise  to come back safely and then they do a  sort of cutesy pinky promise thing that  also is not in the manga so in the space  of almost exactly five minutes the  hunter hunter anime and the hunt hunter  manga have become almost entirely  different stories in the manga gone is  looking for his father a man who was  forced to give up his son due to mito's  actions meanwhile in the anime gon is  looking for his father once again but  he's a man who dumped him on whale  island because he wanted to pursue his  own selfish goals this creates two very  very different impressions of jing one  is a legendary and almost sympathetic  hunter and the other is simply a bit of  a deadbeat dad at the very least i think  that jin could have helped this by doing  a course with the sponsor of today's  video skillshare skillshare is an online  learning community with thousands of  inspiring classes for creative and  curious people explore new skills  develop existing interests and get lost  in creativity recently i've done a  course in productivity for artists  because i'm always looking for new ways  to manage my time efficiently and i've  picked up quite a few handy things to  implement but skillshare is curated  specifically for learning meaning that  there are no ads and they're always  launching new premium classes so you can  stay focused and follow wherever your  creativity takes you skillshare offers  membership with meaning connect with the  support of fellow creatives and enter a  community of encouragement communication  and of course inspiration last the first  1 000 