uch set up to be our  standard wise and powerful shonen mentor  guy now regardless of any changes that  were made in the anime that's well  that's not quite what jing turned out to  be as hunter hunter evolved over the  years so did it saw the yoshihiro  tagashi as did the characters of the  series and arguably even the overall  genre of hunter hunter i would honestly  describe it as more of a seinen story  these days and the character who almost  certainly changed the most over this  time was jing by the time jing actually  made a non-flashback appearance in the  story we had gone through some radical  waves of evolution york new city had  brought us a much darker and more  complex world which greed island and the  chimera antarctic built and expanded on  even more at this stage tagashi was no  longer interested in guiding hunter  hunter down the shonen pathway and very  much like the evolution of his ant  characters the series had become  completely unrecognizable from its  original incarnation and there was no  room for this idealistic and nyon  perfect jing freaks that was presented  in chapter one instead the antithesis  was brought before us jing is portrayed  as a sloppy selfish and pretty seriously  despised figure within the hunter  association and this could not be  further from the almost heroic  description from kite in chapter 1 or  even the general admiration expressed by  satots at the end of the hunter exam  it's a complete subversion of  expectation and not one that was planned  from the beginning but a subversion that  had naturally developed alongside  togashi so much so that when you look  back on the early days of hunter hunter  in general seeing or hearing anything of  jing is like referring to an entirely  different character now when the 2011  anime began they had the advantage of  knowing what hunter hunt would become  unlike tagashi drawing the manga they  had a road map clearly marked with all  the crazy left and yes even sometimes  right 